<%# Layout for the cover / how-to-use / license / about wrapper pages of a
    board printable. A separate layout+template pair rather than a branch
    inside layouts/pdf.html.erb, which backs real users' board exports and
    must stay byte-identical — same rule as pdf_marketing.html.erb.

    This is now the REFERENCE DESIGN for SpeakAnyWay printable wrappers. It
    started as a port of the speakanyway-printables pipeline's wrapper CSS
    (src/templates/wrappers/*.css) and deliberately diverged from it — the
    pipeline is the side that needs to catch up, not the other way round.

    Two rails hold across every change here:

    1. Nothing fetched over the network at render time. Nunito is inlined by
       Boards::Printables::Fonts; a font (or anything else) fetched mid-render
       fails silently into a fallback and nobody notices until it ships.
    2. Every ink-heavy surface has a .ink-light override, because the low-ink
       file's cover renders through this same CSS with that class on <body>.
       The overrides only swap fills for outlines — never sizes — so both
       variants lay out identically and can't disagree about page count. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Board printable</title>

    <style>
      <%= Boards::Printables::Fonts.face_css %>

      :root {
        --navy: #13496f;
        --blue-mid: #0163aa;
        --cyan: #4ECDE6;
        --magenta: #C857E8;
        --cream: #FBF7F1;
        --ink: #1A1A1A;

        --cream-deep: #F3EADC;
        --cyan-tint: #E4F7FB;
        --magenta-tint: #F8EAFD;
        --brand-gradient: linear-gradient(135deg, #4ECDE6 0%, #0163AA 55%, #C857E8 100%);
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      html, body {
        -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
        print-color-adjust: exact;
      }

      body {
        font-family: Nunito, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--cream);
      }

      /* Wrappers are always Letter portrait; the board pages they wrap bring
         their own orientation and the merge preserves it. */
      @page {
        margin: 0;
        size: letter;
      }

      /* Typesetting. Nothing is justified and nothing hyphenates — both produce
         rivers and broken words at these short measures.
         `pretty` costs Chrome a slower line-breaking pass in exchange for
         killing orphans (a stranded last word); `balance` evens the line
         lengths of the short centred blocks — headings, intros, captions —
         where a long-then-tiny break is most obvious. Both are ignored by an
         older Chrome rather than breaking, so the render degrades to the
         default greedy wrap. */
      p, li {
        text-wrap: pretty;
        hyphens: none;
      }

      .cover .title,
      .page-head h2,
      .page-head .intro,
      .about h2,
      .about .quote,
      .pill,
      .qr-card .qr-caption,
      .license-foot p {
        text-wrap: balance;
      }

      /* ── Sheet: the shared 8.5×11 page every wrapper builds on ────────── */
      .sheet {
        width: 8.5in;
        height: 11in;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: var(--cream);
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      .sheet-body {
        flex: 1;
        min-height: 0;
        padding: 0.7in 0.9in 0.55in;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      /* ── Shared primitives ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .band {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        background: var(--brand-gradient);
        color: #fff;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 12pt;
      }

      .band .chip {
        width: 1.5in;
        height: 1.5in;
        background: #fff;
        border-radius: 26%;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
      }

      .band .chip img {
        width: 1.2in;
        height: 1.2in;
      }

      .band .eyebrow {
        color: #fff;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        font-size: 9pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--blue-mid);
      }

      .rule {
        height: 4pt;
        border-radius: 2pt;
        background: var(--brand-gradient);
      }

      .card {
        background: var(--cream-deep);
        border-radius: 12pt;
        padding: 14pt 16pt;
        text-align: left;
      }

      .callout {
        background: var(--cyan-tint);
        border-left: 6pt solid var(--cyan);
        border-radius: 0 10pt 10pt 0;
        padding: 12pt 16pt;
        text-align: left;
      }

      .pill {
        display: inline-block;
        background: var(--cyan-tint);
        color: var(--blue-mid);
        border-radius: 999pt;
        padding: 8pt 22pt;
        font-size: 15pt;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .mark {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 15pt;
        height: 15pt;
        border-radius: 50%;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
      }

      .mark svg {
        width: 9pt;
        height: 9pt;
        stroke: #fff;
        stroke-width: 3.5;
        stroke-linecap: round;
        stroke-linejoin: round;
        fill: none;
      }

      .mark.yes { background: var(--blue-mid); }
      .mark.no  { background: var(--magenta); }

      /* ── Page heading block ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .page-head {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 0.3in;
      }

      .page-head h2 {
        font-size: 34pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin: 6pt 0 12pt;
      }

      .page-head .rule {
        width: 1.6in;
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .page-head .intro {
        font-size: 13pt;
        color: var(--blue-mid);
        line-height: 1.45;
        max-width: 5.6in;
        margin: 14pt auto 0;
      }

      /* ── Cover ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .cover .band {
        height: 2.7in;
      }

      .cover-main {
        flex: 1;
        min-height: 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 0.42in;
        padding: 0.5in 0.75in 0;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .cover .title {
        font-size: 50pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        line-height: 1.08;
        max-width: 6.6in;
      }

      .cover-main .rule {
        width: 1.4in;
      }

      .qr-card {
        background: #fff;
        border-radius: 14pt;
        border: 1pt solid #E7DFD2;
        padding: 16pt 20pt 14pt;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8pt;
      }

      .qr-card img {
        width: 1.15in;
        height: 1.15in;
        display: block;
      }

      .qr-card .qr-caption {
        font-size: 10pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        line-height: 1.25;
      }

      .qr-card .qr-url {
        font-size: 8.5pt;
        color: var(--blue-mid);
      }

      /* Sits under the URL on the about page. Narrower than the card so it
         wraps to two or three short lines instead of one wide one. */
      .qr-card .qr-note {
        font-size: 8.5pt;
        line-height: 1.35;
        color: var(--ink);
        max-width: 2.9in;
        text-align: center;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }

      .cover-footer {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        padding: 0 0.9in 0.55in;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .cover-footer .rule {
        width: 2.2in;
        margin: 0 auto 12pt;
      }

      .cover-footer .brand {
        font-size: 12pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .cover-footer .url {
        font-size: 10pt;
        color: var(--blue-mid);
        margin-top: 3pt;
      }

      /* ── How to use ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* space-between, not start: the six steps never quite fill the page and
         the leftover inch reads as a mistake when it all piles up at the
         bottom. Distributing it between rows looks deliberate at any copy
         length, which matters because the step text changes with @is_set. */
      .steps {
        flex: 1;
        min-height: 0;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 0.18in;
        align-content: space-between;
      }

      .step {
        display: flex;
        gap: 11pt;
        align-items: flex-start;
        background: var(--cream-deep);
        border-radius: 12pt;
        padding: 13pt 15pt;
      }

      .step.wide {
        grid-column: 1 / -1;
      }

      .step .num {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 21pt;
        height: 21pt;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--cyan);
        color: var(--navy);
        font-size: 11pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
      }

      .step .lead {
        font-size: 11.5pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        margin-bottom: 2pt;
      }

      .step p {
        font-size: 10.5pt;
        line-height: 1.42;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .how-to .callout {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        margin-top: 0.22in;
      }

      .how-to .callout p {
        font-size: 11pt;
        line-height: 1.45;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      /* ── What's included (gallery image only, never printed) ─────────── */
      .whats-included .steps {
        align-content: center;
        gap: 0.14in;
      }

      .whats-included .step .lead {
        margin-bottom: 0;
        font-size: 13pt;
      }

      .whats-included .step .num svg {
        width: 12pt;
        height: 12pt;
        fill: var(--navy);
      }

      .whats-included .callout {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        margin-top: 0.22in;
      }

      .whats-included .callout p {
        font-size: 11.5pt;
        line-height: 1.45;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      /* ── License ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      /* One centred column. Each term is a whole sentence, so a narrow
         side-by-side column squeezed them to three and four lines each with
         a stranded last word; at full measure they all fit on one or two. */
      .terms {
        flex: 1;
        min-height: 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 26pt;
        width: 5.9in;
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .terms li {
        list-style: none;
        display: flex;
        gap: 14pt;
        align-items: flex-start;
        font-size: 14pt;
        line-height: 1.45;
        text-align: left;
      }

      .terms .mark {
        /* Optical alignment with the cap height of the first line, not the
           line box — a flex-start mark sits visibly high next to 13pt text. */
        margin-top: 2.5pt;
      }

      .license-foot {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .license-foot .rule {
        width: 1.6in;
        margin: 0 auto 12pt;
      }

      .license-foot p {
        font-size: 10pt;
        color: var(--blue-mid);
      }

      /* ── About ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .about .band {
        height: 1.5in;
      }

      .about .band .chip {
        width: 1in;
        height: 1in;
      }

      .about .band .chip img {
        width: 0.8in;
        height: 0.8in;
      }

      /* Centred rather than top-aligned: the About copy is short and a
         bottom-pinned sign-off left a dead inch under the QR card. */
      .about .sheet-body {
        justify-content: center;
      }

      .about h2 {
        font-size: 32pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 0.28in;
      }

      .about .quote {
        border-left: 6pt solid var(--cyan);
        padding: 4pt 0 4pt 16pt;
        font-size: 20pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        line-height: 1.25;
        color: var(--navy);
        margin-bottom: 0.28in;
      }

      .about p.body {
        font-size: 12pt;
        line-height: 1.55;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .about .cta {
        font-size: 12pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--navy);
        margin-top: 0.22in;
      }

      .about .qr-card {
        align-self: center;
        margin-top: 0.3in;
      }

      .about .qr-card img {
        width: 1.35in;
        height: 1.35in;
      }

      .thanks {
        padding-top: 0.4in;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 12pt;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--magenta);
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 7pt;
      }

      /* An SVG heart, not the emoji — headless Chrome on the render box has no
         guaranteed colour-emoji font, so the glyph is a tofu-box risk. This
         comment ships in the rendered HTML, so it can't contain one either. */
      .thanks svg {
        width: 13pt;
        height: 13pt;
        fill: var(--magenta);
      }

      /* ── Ink-light: fills become outlines, geometry never moves ───────── */
      .ink-light .sheet,
      .ink-light .band {
        background: #fff;
      }

      /* Bottom edge only. A gradient rule flush against the top of the sheet
         reads as a printer artifact, not as a design. */
      .ink-light .band {
        color: var(--navy);
        border-bottom: 5pt solid transparent;
        border-image: var(--brand-gradient) 1;
      }

      .ink-light .band .chip {
        background: transparent;
      }

      .ink-light .band .eyebrow {
        color: var(--blue-mid);
      }

      /* Only the cover renders ink-light today, so .pill and .qr-card are the
         two that matter. The rest are here so the rule above stays true if
         another page ever gets an ink-light variant — .terms .card is listed
         explicitly because its tint selector out-specifies a bare .card. */
      .ink-light .pill,
      .ink-light .qr-card,
      .ink-light .step,
      .ink-light .card,
      .ink-light .terms .card,
      .ink-light .callout {
        background: #fff;
        border: 1pt solid var(--cyan);
      }

    </style>
  </head>

  <%# This layout prints, and only prints. The marketplace gallery used to
      render through it too, with .as-listing-image scaling the sheet onto a
      square mat — honest, and invisible next to purpose-built competitor art.
      The slides now have their own canvas in layouts/listing_image.html.erb,
      which is free to be a marketing surface without any of the rules above
      having to hold for it.

      Joined rather than interpolated side by side: a stray space here changes
      the rendered attribute for every PDF page, and the wrapper specs pin it. %>
  <body class="<%= [("ink-light" if @ink_light)].compact.join(" ") %>">
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
